1. High-Level Overview (30 seconds)

"Sleep Detector is a Windows desktop application that continuously monitors the user's face through the webcam. It uses MediaPipe Face Landmarker to detect facial landmarks around the eyes in real time. By calculating the Eye Aspect Ratio (EAR), it determines whether the eyes are open or closed. If the eyes remain closed beyond a predefined threshold, the application considers the user drowsy and plays an alarm. The application runs in the background using a system tray icon and can be installed like a normal Windows application."

