3. Explain each module
main.py

"main.py is the bootstrap file. It creates all the application components, connects them together, starts the GUI, launches the system tray, and ensures that everything shuts down safely when the user exits."

gui.py

"This module contains the graphical interface built with CustomTkinter. It lets the user start or stop monitoring, displays logs, and changes settings."

detector.py

"This is the core of the application. It captures webcam frames using OpenCV, sends them to MediaPipe for face landmark detection, calculates the eye state, and triggers the alarm if drowsiness is detected."

tray.py

"This module creates the Windows system tray icon using pystray. It allows the application to keep running in the background even when the main window is hidden."

logger.py

"It records important events such as monitoring started, sleep detected, user awake, and monitoring stopped into a log file."

settings_manager.py

"This module reads and writes the application's configuration, such as alarm settings and thresholds, to a JSON file."

